## Highlights
- In May, a student in New Zealand confessed to using AI to write their papers, justifying it as a tool like Grammarly or spell-check: ​​“I have the knowledge, I have the lived experience, I’m a good student, I go to all the tutorials and I go to all the lectures and I read everything we have to read but I kind of felt I was being penalised because I don’t write eloquently and I didn’t feel that was right,” [they told a student paper](https://www.canta.co.nz/newsarticle/115524?newsfeedId=1453013) in Christchurch. They don’t feel like they’re cheating, because the student guidelines at their university state only that you’re not allowed to get somebody else to do your work for you. GPT-3 isn’t “somebody else”—it’s a program. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01j1gpjh2kt8rqswpqgcnxr7e8))
